# Build-time values for the deployed site, read by `vite build`.
#
# These are committed deliberately. Vite bakes every VITE_ value into the
# public JS bundle, so all six are readable by anyone who opens the deployed
# site regardless of where they are stored - keeping them in a GitHub secret
# would hide them from this file and from nowhere else. Committing them means
# the build needs no repository configuration at all.
#
# What actually protects the account is NOT the secrecy of these strings:
#   - Firestore security rules + Firebase Auth guard the data.
#   - The EmailJS domain allowlist (Account > Security) is what stops someone
#     sending mail through your account with the keys below.
# Keep both of those tight. Never put a genuine secret - anything with write
# or delete power that no rule checks - in a VITE_ variable.

VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=AIzaSyCvSvOt1WH25061LZruhZdx9epXugenDZA
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=vr-backend-passkey.firebaseapp.com
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=vr-backend-passkey

VITE_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=vaGa2A8eS_8F7Ln9w
VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=service_6hu9tjg
VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=template_subcoui
